Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:05:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 050/106] media: qcom: camss: fix a typo in sm7150's cphy_rx
 clock rates

vfe0_cphy_rx lists 38400000 where every other rate list in this file, the
two entries right below it included, spells the same rate 384000000.

camcc-sm7150 only offers 19.2, 300, 384 and 400MHz on this clock, so the
typo does not name a rate the hardware has, and it leaves the list out of
order: the rate picker walks it front to back looking for the first entry
above the minimum, so 384MHz - the rate the vendor device tree asks for
at its lowest performance level - can never be selected.

Fixes: 22240b4941e2 ("media: qcom: camss: Add sm7150 resources")
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 141d04169..d18b0aefc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -1844,7 +1844,7 @@ static const struct camss_subdev_resources vfe_res_7150[] = {
 				{ /*19200000, 380000000,*/ 510000000, 637000000, 760000000 },
 				{ /*19200000, 380000000,*/ 510000000, 637000000, 760000000 },
 				{ 0 },
-				{ 19200000, 300000000, 38400000, 400000000 },
+				{ 19200000, 300000000, 384000000, 400000000 },
 				{ 19200000, 75000000, 300000000, 384000000, 400000000 },
 				{ 19200000, 75000000, 300000000, 384000000, 400000000 },
 				{ 19200000, 150000000, 240000000, 320000000, 400000000, 480000000 },
